=====================================================================
ABSTRACT

This project presents a multi-layer secure electronic voting system designed to improve voter authentication, process transparency, and operational control. The system combines QR-based booth verification, face verification, and blockchain-supported vote auditability. The proposed workflow requires a voter to pass sequential checks: registration, QR generation, booth scan and admin approval, face verification, and then vote casting. The architecture includes a frontend voting portal, Node.js backend API, dedicated QR service module, Python Flask face verification service, and smart-contract deployment over Ganache using Truffle.

The project also introduces practical admin capabilities such as candidate management, voter statistics, QR approval handling, live voting updates, and election restart/reset control. Experimental testing demonstrates that only authenticated voters can proceed to vote, invalid biometric attempts are rejected, and audit visibility improves election trust. The solution is suitable for educational/institutional election scenarios and can be extended with liveness detection, stronger persistence layers, and production-grade deployment.

Keywords: E-voting, QR verification, Face verification, JWT, Blockchain, Ganache, Truffle, Admin Dashboard

